Don't make usleep a NOFORK applet on WIN32.
On WIN32 a NOFORK applet runs inside the shell process, and Sleep()
can't be interrupted, so ^C during "usleep N" in the shell only took
effect after the whole pause. (On Linux, nanosleep() returns early on
SIGINT.) Make usleep a normal applet on WIN32, as sleep already is, so
that it runs in its own process and ^C ends it at once.

---
 coreutils/usleep.c |    8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/usleep.c
+++ b/coreutils/usleep.c
@@ -12,7 +12,15 @@
 //config:	help
 //config:	usleep is used to pause for a specified number of microseconds.
 
+// NOTE: For WIN32 this applet is not NOFORK: Sleep() can't be interrupted,
+//       so ^C in a shell would only take effect after the pause.
+
+//applet:IF_PLATFORM_MINGW32(
+//applet:IF_USLEEP(APPLET(usleep, BB_DIR_BIN, BB_SUID_DROP))
+//applet:)
+//applet:IF_PLATFORM_POSIX(
 //applet:IF_USLEEP(APPLET_NOFORK(usleep, usleep, BB_DIR_BIN, BB_SUID_DROP, usleep))
+//applet:)
 
 //kbuild:lib-$(CONFIG_USLEEP) += usleep.o
 
